{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-ecc-8-1","title":"Ecclesiastes 8:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 True wisdom is modest. 2 Kings are to be respected. 6 Divine providence is to be observed. 12 It is better with the godly in adversity, than with the wicked in prosperity. 16 The work of God is unsearchable.</p>\n<p>as the 2:13,14; 1Co 2:13-16 who knoweth. Ge 40:8; 41:15,16,38,39; Job 33:23; Pr 1:6; Da 2:28-30,47; 4:18,19 2Pe 1:20 a man's. Ex 34:29,30; Pr 4:8,9; 17:24; 24:5; Mt 17:2; Ac 6:15 and the. De 28:50; Ac 4:13,29; Eph 6:19 boldness. Heb. strength. 2Ti 4:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-8-2","title":"Ecclesiastes 8:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>I counsel. Pr 24:21; Ro 13:1-4; Tit 3:1; 1Pe 2:13-17 in regard. 1Ki 2:43; 1Ch 29:24; Eze 17:13-20; Ro 13:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-8-3","title":"Ecclesiastes 8:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>not hasty. 10:4; Pr 14:29 stand. 1Ki 1:50-52; 2:21-24; Isa 48:4; Jer 44:16,17; Ac 5:8,9 for. Pr 16:14,15; 30:31; Da 4:35; 5:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-8-4","title":"Ecclesiastes 8:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>the word. 1Ki 2:25,29-34,46; Pr 19:12; 20:2; 30:31; Da 3:15; Lu 12:4,5 Ro 13:1-4 What. Job 33:12,13; 34:18,19; Ro 9:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-8-5","title":"Ecclesiastes 8:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>keepeth. 2; Ex 1:17,20,21; Ps 119:6; Ho 5:11; Lu 20:25; Ac 4:19; 5:29 Ro 13:5-7; 1Pe 3:13,14 feel. Heb. know. a wise. 2:14; 10:2; 1Ch 12:32; Pr 17:24; Lu 12:56,57; 1Co 2:14,15 Php 1:9,10; Col 1:9; Heb 5:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-8-6","title":"Ecclesiastes 8:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>to every. 3:1,11,17; 7:13,14 therefore. 11:9,10; 12:1; Isa 3:11-14; 22:12-14; Lu 13:25; 17:26-30; 19:42-44 Heb 3:7-11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-8-7","title":"Ecclesiastes 8:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>he knoweth. 6:12; 9:12; 10:14; Pr 24:22; 29:1; Mt 24:44,50; 25:6-13; 1Th 5:1-3 when. or, how.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-8-8","title":"Ecclesiastes 8:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>is no. 3:21; 2Sa 14:14; Job 14:5; 34:14; Ps 49:6-9; 89:48; Heb 9:27 power. 1Co 15:43; 2Co 13:4 discharge. or, casting off weapons. De 20:1-8; 2Ki 7:15 neither. Ps 9:17; 52:5-7; 73:18-28; Pr 14:32; Isa 28:15,18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-8-9","title":"Ecclesiastes 8:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>this. 1:14; 3:10; 4:7,8; 7:25 there is. 5:8,13; Ex 14:5-9,28; De 2:30; 2Ki 14:10-12; 25:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-8-10","title":"Ecclesiastes 8:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>so. 2Ki 9:34,35; Job 21:18,32,33; Lu 16:22 the place. Ps 122:1-5; Ac 6:13 they were. 2:16; 9:5; Ps 31:12; Pr 10:7; Jer 17:13; Heb 10:38</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-8-11","title":"Ecclesiastes 8:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>sentence. Ex 8:15,32; Job 21:11-15; Ps 10:6; 50:21,22; Isa 5:18,19; 26:10 Isa 57:11; Jer 48:11; Mt 24:49,50; Ro 2:4,5; 2Pe 3:3-10 fully. Jer 42:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-8-12","title":"Ecclesiastes 8:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>a sinner. 5:16; 7:15; 1Ki 2:5-9; 21:25; 22:34,35; Pr 13:21; Isa 65:20; Ro 2:5 Ro 9:22; 2Pe 2:9 surely. 7:18; Ps 37:11,18,19; 112:1; 115:13; Pr 1:32,33; Isa 3:10,11 Isa 65:13,14,20-24; Mt 25:34,41-46; Lu 1:50 fear before. 3:14; 1Ch 16:30; Ps 96:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-8-13","title":"Ecclesiastes 8:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>it shall. Job 18:5; 20:5; 21:30; Ps 11:5; Isa 57:21; Mal 3:18; Mt 13:49,50 Joh 5:29 neither. Ps 55:23; Isa 30:13; 2Pe 2:3 as a. 6:12; Job 7:6,7; 14:2; Ps 39:5; 144:4; Jas 4:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-8-14","title":"Ecclesiastes 8:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>a vanity. 4:4,8; 9:3; 10:5 there be just. 2:14; 7:15; 9:1-3; Job 9:22-24; 21:17-34; 24:21-25; Ps 73:13,14 Mal 3:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-8-15","title":"Ecclesiastes 8:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>Then I.Some consider this as the cavil of an infidel objector, equivalent to the Epicurean maxim, {Ede, bibe, lude; post mortem nulla voluptas,} \"Eat, drink, and play; there is no pleasure after death.\" But it may be regarded as a recommendation of a moderate use of worldly things, with a cheerful and contented mind; which may justly be considered as the greatest advantage which can be made of all below the sun: and amidst all changes, such a frame of mind, if the result of right principles, may and ought to be preserved; and it will be the recompence and solace of all our labours and toils.</p>\n<p>2:24; 3:12,13,22; 5:18; 9:7-9; 1Ti 4:3,4; 6:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-8-16","title":"Ecclesiastes 8:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>When I.Solomon here records the result of his perplexing inquiries into the affairs of men, and the purposes, providence, and works of God. And when he examined with great attention and diligence into the works of God, he found he could neither comprehend nor explain them; and was persuaded, that no application or capacity would enable a man to fathom the depth of the Divine dispensations in this lower world. How vain, then, are all cavils against Divine providence; when we can neither understand, nor comprehend it!</p>\n<p>9; 7; 7:25 there is that. 2:23; 4:8; 5:12; Ge 31:40; Ps 127:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ecc-8-17","title":"Ecclesiastes 8:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ECC","chapterStart":8,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":8,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>that a man. 3:11; 7:23,24; 11:5; Job 5:9; 11:7-9; Ps 40:5; 73:16; 104:24 Pr 30:3,4; Isa 40:28; Ro 11:33</p>"}]}